<title>DENMARK: Danish BG Bank 1997 H1 profit climbs.</title>
<headline>Danish BG Bank 1997 H1 profit climbs.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax result		 1.063 vs 821</p>
<p> Securities and forex results	 279 vs 118</p>
<p> Losses and bad debt provisions    175  vs 297</p>
<p> Pre-tax &amp; ex.items profit     1,250 vs   847</p>
<p>Net interest and fees income  3,194 vs 3,038  Result of financial items     3,566 vs 3,263</p>
<p> Own capital end-June 1997     7,847 vs 6,602 end-June 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's third biggest bank is BG Bank A/S. It said in a statement that it expected higher full year 1997 core earnings than in 1996. The result exceeded analysts' expectations of an average 1.177 billion crown first-half 1997 result before tax and extraordinary items.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
</text>
